title: The German October
subtitle: In Moscow, the Politburo decides that the German revolution is near.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 9 and e23_october_path = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_oct_directive = 0;
if (Q.comintern_member == 1) {
    // effort stays below what would close the directive by itself: the October's own end decides it
    RG.directive({
        id: 'october', title: 'The German October',
        text: 'The Executive instructs the German section to prepare the armed rising: to fix the date, to arm the proletarian hundreds, to enter the governments of Saxony and Thuringia as the base of the revolution, and to give the signal when the Reichswehr marches.',
        from: 'trotsky', months: 3,
        goals: [{q: 'e23_rising_phase', op: '=', v: 1}],
        reward: {funds: 3, favour: 20, faction: 'offensive'},
        punish: 'rival', announce: false
    });
    Q.e23_oct_directive = 1;
}
RG.news('German communist leaders summoned to Moscow', 2);
var L = {unionist: 'Heinrich Brandler', offensive: 'Ruth Fischer', luxemburgist: (Q.luxemburg_alive == 1 ? 'Rosa Luxemburg' : (Q.levi_in_party == 1 ? 'Paul Levi' : 'Ernst Meyer')), ultraleft: 'Karl Schröder'};
Q.party_leader = L[Q.leading_faction];
Q.lead_code = {luxemburgist: 1, offensive: 2, unionist: 3, ultraleft: 4}[Q.leading_faction];
!}

= The German October

On 23 August, after the Cuno strike, the Politburo in Moscow decided that Germany is ripe. Trotsky, Zinoviev, Radek and Stalin argued over the details and agreed on the essentials: the German party must prepare an armed rising, Moscow will pay for it, and Russian officers will help to plan it. Since September, [+ party_leader +] and the German leaders have been in Moscow for weeks of meetings.

Trotsky wants a date, fixed in advance, as in Petrograd: he proposes 9 November, the anniversary of the German revolution. Brandler says the German party, not the Russian, must decide the moment, and asks for Trotsky himself to come to Germany to lead it. Zinoviev wants a rising and is not sure he wants Trotsky to have the credit. [? if lead_code = 2 : Ruth Fischer, for the Left, says the party is ready now. ?]

[? if warsaw_outcome = 2 : Since 1920, the Red Army has stood on the Vistula. If Germany rises, Trotsky says, it will not be alone. ?]

The plan is simple to describe. The party will enter the governments of Saxony and Thuringia, arm the hundreds from the state arsenals, and when the Reichswehr marches on Saxony, a general strike will turn into a rising across the Reich.

- @date: Accept the plan, and Trotsky's date.
- @own_moment: Accept the plan, but the German party chooses the moment.
- @now: The moment is now: rise in October, before the enemy is ready.
- @refuse: Refuse: the German working class is not ready for power.

@date
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Moscow's plan in full. Money, arms and advisers; little room for our own judgement.
on-arrival: {!
RG.comply(25);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
Q.comintern_rep = 'Karl Radek';
RG.setRole('radek', 'Envoy of the Executive, in Germany for the October');
RG.ledger('Accepted Moscow\'s plan for a German October, and Trotsky\'s date.', 'e23_plan');
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e23_october_path = 1;
Q.e23_date_set = 1;
Q.independence -= 10;
Q.resources += 3;
Q.red_guards_arms += 6;
Q.moscow_subsidy += 1;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

The date is set and written in no document. Pyatakov and Radek leave for Berlin with false papers. Red Army officers follow, and money, a great deal of it.

@own_moment
subtitle: The Right's answer. Moscow's help, on German terms. Trotsky is annoyed.
on-arrival: {!
RG.comply(15);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -6);
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
Q.comintern_rep = 'Karl Radek';
RG.setRole('radek', 'Envoy of the Executive, in Germany for the October');
RG.ledger('Accepted Moscow\'s plan for a German October, on German terms.', 'e23_plan');
Q.e23_october_path = 1;
Q.e23_date_set = 0;
Q.independence -= 4;
Q.resources += 2;
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Moscow agrees that the Germans will give the signal. Trotsky is not sent. Radek and Pyatakov are, and a group of Red Army officers to plan the military side.

@now
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's answer. Less preparation, more surprise.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.comply(25);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 8);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -2);
RG.ledger('Committed the party to a rising in October 1923.', 'e23_plan');
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e23_october_path = 1;
Q.e23_hasty = 1;
Q.independence -= 4;
Q.resources += 2;
Q.militancy += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 8;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

The Left's resolution wins in Moscow over Brandler's objections. The rising will come in October, with whatever arms there are.

@refuse
subtitle: The Spartacist verdict. Independence rises sharply; Moscow's money and patience run out.
on-arrival: {!
RG.defy();
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -10);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -10);
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
Q.e23_october_path = 0;
Q.independence += 10;
Q.moscow_subsidy = Math.max(0, Q.moscow_subsidy - 1);
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 12;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 8;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
Q.world_revolution -= 5;
!}

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg writes the German reply. A revolution, she writes, cannot be ordered for a date like a delivery of coal. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : The German delegation says no, politely and then less politely. ?] Zinoviev calls it the gravest error since Levi. Radek, privately, is relieved.
